                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote><p>Very carefully and neatly carved, widely spaced letters, with a narrow simple v-cut and without serifs. Alpha with straight bar; beta with equal closed loops; epsilon with shorter middle bar; theta is small, circular, above the line, with a central dot (32 mm); kappa has nearly full length equal arms; nu is enitrely regular; omicron is small and above the line (25-27 mm); pi has a shorter right hasta, and the cross-bar does not overextend; rho has a large closed loop; sigma has slightly open outer strokes; omega is almost full size, nearly circular, open with horizontal feet.</p>
