                        <provenance type="found" subtype="discovered" notAfter="1734">The base appears to have been found in Acradina in 1734. Lupi 1734, the first published notice, merely refers to it as a 'basis nuper inventa Syracusis'. However, a fuller account of Lupi is provided in Schiavo 1756 (vol.1.5, p.17), stating that it was found in 1734 in the modern suburbs of Siracusa but within the ancient walls. This is in turn formulated as the part of Acradina close to the two ports of the city in the epigraphic 'Raccolta' of Cesare Gaetani (Syracusan antiquarian, 1718-1808, the manuscript compiled 1772-1784).<geo cert="medium">37.0663903,15.2833471</geo></provenance><!-- generic location in Achradina, vague vicinity of the Agora?-->
